# Local trained models

Provide these real trained model artifacts before using prediction endpoints:

| Required artifact | Development notebook |
| --- | --- |
| diabetes_xgb_final.pkl | notebooks/MediRisk_Diabetes_Analysis.ipynb |
| diabetes2_xgb_model.pkl | notebooks/Diabetes2_Analysis.ipynb |
| heart_xgb_model.pkl | notebooks/MediRisk_HeartDisease_Analysis..ipynb |

`backend/predict.py` loads all three together on its first import. Restore
compatible artifacts from your local project backup or train/export them from
the notebooks with the required datasets and dependencies.

The project also has diabetes_rf_model.pkl and diabetes2_label_encoder.pkl for
model development. These are not loaded by the current prediction backend.

Do not rename this template to `.pkl`; it is documentation, not a serialized
model. Real model files are intentionally excluded from Git.
